1. Find the IDs of dogs that have received more than two treatments.
2. Identify the professionals who have treated these dogs.
3. Retrieve the details (ID, last name, cell number) of these professionals from Indiana.

```sql
1. SELECT dog_id FROM Treatments GROUP BY dog_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 2;
2. SELECT professional_id FROM Treatments WHERE dog_id IN (SELECT dog_id FROM Treatments GROUP BY dog_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 2);
3. SELECT professional_id, last_name, cell_number FROM Professionals WHERE state = 'Indiana' AND professional_id IN (SELECT professional_id FROM Treatments WHERE dog_id IN (SELECT dog_id FROM Treatments GROUP BY dog_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 2));
```

